+/** Number of samples the lossy coder adds to each side of a chunk before
+ *  coding it.
+ *
+ *  The chunk is coded as an independent JPEG 2000 image, so the first and
+ *  last row and column of the chunk sit on the boundary of the wavelet
+ *  transform and are reconstructed with noticeably more distortion than
+ *  interior samples.  The coded image is therefore grown by this many
+ *  samples on all four sides, filled by continuing the chunk outward from
+ *  its edge samples, which keeps every image sample away from the transform
+ *  boundary.  The decoder discards the added samples.
+ *
+ *  Codestreams that code the chunk exactly, as written for lossless coding
+ *  and by earlier writers, remain readable. */
+static const int32_t LJ2K_BOUNDARY_PAD = 16;
+
